__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
data/raw/
data/processed/
# Trained models are excluded by default, except the ones the shipped config points at: without
# them a fresh clone cannot run the pipeline at all. `boundary_tabme` is the shipped default
# (English) and MUST stay included -- omitting it once already produced a repository whose config
# named a model the clone did not contain. `boundary_shortpackets` is the documented Dutch
# alternative. The experimental variants from the ablations (boundary_openpss_v2/_prior/_flow,
# boundary_rvlcdip, boundary_cross_encoder*) stay out -- they are reproducible from scripts/.
models/*
!models/boundary_tabme/
!models/boundary_openpss/
!models/boundary_shortpackets/
!models/document_classifier/

# Generated outputs are excluded by default, except the submission deliverables: the benchmark
# reports (Deliverable 6) and representative sample outputs (Deliverable 7). Note `outputs/*`
# rather than `outputs/` -- git cannot re-include a child of an excluded directory, so the
# directory itself must stay traversable for the negations below to apply.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/benchmarks/
!outputs/error_analysis/
!outputs/benchmark_status.md
!outputs/api_response_benchmark.json

# Sample outputs: keep the structured artifacts, drop the bulky intermediates (page renders and
# the dense vector dump) which are reproducible and carry no review value.
!outputs/sample_packet_check/
outputs/sample_packet_check/rendered_pages/
outputs/sample_packet_check/index/

# CatBoost writes training logs to the working directory
catboost_info/
